  "rules": [
    "Store Godot asset identifiers/paths rather than binary mesh data in botanical JSON.",
    "Re-use base models, rigs, materials and animations by reference; cultivar differences belong in variant_overrides or dedicated stage assets.",
    "Stages are species-dependent; avoid forcing annual senescence or woody dormancy onto every taxon.",
    "Keep chronological growth and phenological states distinct: flowering/fruiting may recur after maturity and can overlap.",
    "Do not invent missing renders or mark assets approved without visual inspection.",
    "Asset paths must be project-relative and validated before gameplay integration.",
    "The spreadsheet is a review surface, not a live asset repository; integrate via audited import."
